---
description: Git hooks rules and commit/push enforcement
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---
- NEVER use `--no-verify` or `-n` flags to bypass git hooks.
- Pre-commit checks must always pass before committing.
- Pre-push checks must always pass before pushing.
- If checks fail, fix the issues rather than bypassing hooks.
- Pre-commit hook enforces code quality, formatting, linting, and tests.
- Pre-push hook ensures all pre-commit checks pass before allowing push.
- All commits must follow Conventional Commits format.
- Git hooks are mandatory and cannot be skipped.